node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.next
**/.next
# The LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR working directory — never the source tree.
#
# This was `storage` + `**/storage`, and `**/storage` also matched
# `apps/web/src/app/api/storage/`, so `GET /api/storage/:path*` was silently
# absent from every web image ever built. Nobody noticed while production served
# assets straight from R2's public base url and this route only mattered in dev
# — but the moment `upload()` started returning `/api/storage/<key>`
# (26a0f34), every asset link in production 404'd. Found 2026-08-16 by probing
# the deployed container: `.next/server/app/api` listed nine routes and not this
# one.
#
# Anchored patterns only, so a directory NAMED storage anywhere in the source
# tree keeps travelling into the image.
/storage
apps/*/storage
*.log
# Root AND nested. dockerignore patterns are NOT recursive: plain `.env` matches
# only the context root, so apps/web/.env and apps/worker/.env were being copied
# into the image with every server secret in them (found 2026-08-14). The web
# build genuinely needs the two NEXT_PUBLIC_* values — those now arrive as build
# args instead; everything else reaches the container at RUNTIME via env_file.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
